  "section_notes": "The final v13 text sets a 24-hour incident reporting rule and keeps per-model test results away from the general public while giving them to purchasers and regulators. The S2 transition (36 months to bring existing models into compliance, with a 5% permanent limit) favours Northwind's Hearth 10, and the 24-month new-unit shut-off deadline falls outside the acceptable range. The S5 recall trigger of 8 per 100,000 is mandatory with no transition, which directly constrains Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9."
